;;; host-effects-contract.mon --- Real engine integration-gated regression Execute through the embedded Monad test runner, not an isolated parser.

:author Laluxx
:version 0.1.0
:keywords obsidian tests contract host-effects-contract

;;; Commentary:

host-effects-contract.mon — Real engine integration-gated regression
Required assertions for the host harness:
1. During image publication (engine-mutable?) is False; scene
node-visible!, camera-move!, mesh-visible!, sdf-material! reject.
2. At an active callback (engine-mutable?) is True; only valid borrowed
objects accept writes, and the engine remains owner of all storage.
3. A rejected image with a staged invalid/native-owned key chord MUST
not alter the live keymap or installed frame callback.
4. An ended Frame capability MUST fail, even if held in a Monad value.
5. Leak-check retained native images across repeated failures.
The native effect-policy test checks only the host phase matrix.

;;; Code:
(define (engine-effect-observation)
  (list (engine-mutable?) (engine-gpu-mutable?)))
